 I'll discard T1.\n\nReason: T1 is a terminal tile with limited connectivity in the current hand, as it only pairs with another T1 or forms a sequence with T2 and T3, but I have only one T2 and no T3. Discarding it improves tile efficiency and keeps options open for forming sequences in the W and B suits, where I have more tiles and potential melds. Keeping the B9 triplet is valuable for future points, and the W2-W3-W4 sequence is promising. This discard aligns with aiming for a hand that can score through combinations like All Simples (if I eventually get rid of B9) or mixed patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play T1"}
