 for sequences and doesn\u2019t give away dangerous tiles.  \n**Best discards**:  \n- W2 or W3: since W2 and W3 already used in meld, keeping them is useless for hand building; they\u2019re safe discards (W2: 3 left, W3: 3 left).  \n- F1: keeping may give Seat Wind pung if lucky, but only 3 left unshown, low chance.  \n- Among B singles, B4 is least useful because B4 is dead (across player melded B3-B4-B5, only 2 left unseen). B6 (4 left) and B7 (4 left) maybe keep for chow chances. B2 (4 left) is simple tile, maybe keep if going for All Simples but B9 prevents it anyway.  \n.  \nGiven all, discard **W2** or **W3** is harmless and doesn\u2019t break B suit structure.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nW2 and W3 are already part of the exposed Chow meld, so they have no further use in hand. Discarding them now is safe and avoids giving away potentially useful B suit tiles that could form chows/pungs later. Among the two, W2 has 3 left unseen, W3 also 3 left, similar safety.  \nDiscarding B9 would break a potential pung; B8 and B7 could be kept for possible chow with B6-B7-B8 if drawn more. F1 kept for potential Seat Wind pung.  \nThus, best: **Play W2**.\n\n**Answer:** Play W2"}
