ile efficiency:  \nWe have B6(2), B7(1), B8(2), B9(3).  \nWe want to maximize bamboo chows/pungs:  \nB6,B7,B8 chow possible if draw B7.  \nB7,B8,B9 chow possible if draw B7.  \nB8,B9 chow not possible (need B9 pair already triple).  \nB9 pung possible.  \n\nSo best to keep B7 for connectivity.  \n\nThus discard among W2, W3, F1.  \n\nF1 discard gives All Simples path (2 pts) but loses Pung of Terminals/Honors (1 pt) and Prevalent Wind/Seat Wind chances.  \nPrevalent Wind: South (F2), Seat Wind: East (F1).  \nSo F1 is **Seat Wind** \u2192 keeping F1 could give Seat Wind pung (2 pts) if we get two more F1. Unseen F1: 3 left. Possible.  \n\nSo maybe keep F1 for now, discard W2 or W3.  \n\nBetween W2 and W3:  \nW2 connects to W1,W3 for chow but we already have W2,W3,W4 exposed, so extra W2 useless unless pair.  \nW3 same.  \n\nChoose W3 because only 1 left unseen, harder to pair, discard now.  \n\n---\n\n**Reason**:  \nDiscard W3 keeps W2 for possible pair (2 left unseen), keeps F1 for Seat Wind pung chance, keeps all Bamboo for Half Flush or All Simples flexibility.  \n\n**Answer**: Play W3"}
